        <UserObject label="&lt;div style=&quot;width:336px;height:210px;color:#0B1324;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:36px;line-height:36px;font-size:30px;font-weight:bold;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;Connected&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;height:44px;line-height:44px;font-size:32px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;المتصل&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:24px;margin:6px 0px 8px 0px;display:flex;align-items:center;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;flex:1;height:1px;background-color:#826730;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;flex:none;box-sizing:border-box;width:132px;height:24px;line-height:20px;border-radius:12px;border:2px solid #0B1324;color:#0B1324;font-size:14px;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;4 or 5 counts&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;flex:1;height:1px;background-color:#826730;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:92px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;justify-content:center;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:14px;line-height:20px;text-align:center;text-wrap:balance;&quot;&gt;The hamzah is in the same word as the long vowel.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:30px;line-height:30px;margin-top:2px;text-align:center;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:13px;font-style:italic;margin-right:10px;&quot;&gt;like&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;unicode-bidi:isolate;font-size:20px;&quot;&gt;جَآءَ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:20px;margin:0px 10px;&quot;&gt;·&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;unicode-bidi:isolate;font-size:20px;&quot;&gt;قُرُوٓءٍ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:20px;margin:0px 10px;&quot;&gt;·&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;unicode-bidi:isolate;font-size:20px;&quot;&gt;هَنِيٓئًا&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" tooltip="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:19px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Connected&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:4px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;All of these conditions apply, top box first:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Vowel Lengthening: A long vowel or a soft letter is held.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Secondary: The lengthening has a cause, one of two: a hamzah right before or right after the letter, or a sukūn on the next letter.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Caused by hamzah: The cause is a hamzah right before or right after the letter, and the letter is a long vowel.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Hamzah after: The hamzah comes right after the long vowel.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Connected:&lt;/b&gt; The hamzah is in the same word as the long vowel.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Length:&lt;/b&gt; 4 or 5 counts, set by the box “Hamzah after”.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:4px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Examples:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:30px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:19px;&quot;&gt;جَآءَ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;alif · an-Naṣr 110:1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:30px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:19px;&quot;&gt;قُرُوٓءٍ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;wāw · al-Baqarah 2:228&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:30px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:19px;&quot;&gt;هَنِيٓئًا&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;yāʾ · an-Nisāʾ 4:4&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:2px;&quot;&gt;One exception to the 4 or 5 counts: if the word ends in the hamzah and you stop on the word, as in &lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:17px;&quot;&gt;السَّمَآءِ&lt;/span&gt;, the length may be 4, 5 or 6 counts, but not 2.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" id="muttasil">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=28;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F6B93B;strokeColor=#FAD893;strokeWidth=2;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#0B1324;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=10;shadow=0;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="230" width="360" x="40" y="1400" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="&lt;div style=&quot;width:336px;height:210px;color:#0B1324;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:36px;line-height:36px;font-size:30px;font-weight:bold;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;Separated&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;height:44px;line-height:44px;font-size:32px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;المنفصل&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:24px;margin:6px 0px 8px 0px;display:flex;align-items:center;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;flex:1;height:1px;background-color:#826730;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;flex:none;box-sizing:border-box;width:132px;height:24px;line-height:20px;border-radius:12px;border:2px solid #0B1324;color:#0B1324;font-size:14px;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;4 or 5 counts&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;flex:1;height:1px;background-color:#826730;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:92px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;justify-content:center;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:14px;line-height:20px;text-align:center;text-wrap:balance;&quot;&gt;The hamzah begins the next word: the long vowel ends one word, and you do not stop between them.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:30px;line-height:30px;margin-top:2px;text-align:center;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:13px;font-style:italic;margin-right:10px;&quot;&gt;like&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;unicode-bidi:isolate;font-size:20px;&quot;&gt;بِمَآ أُنْزِلَ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:20px;margin:0px 10px;&quot;&gt;·&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;unicode-bidi:isolate;font-size:20px;&quot;&gt;قُوٓا أَنْفُسَكُمْ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:20px;margin:0px 10px;&quot;&gt;·&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;unicode-bidi:isolate;font-size:20px;&quot;&gt;وَفِيٓ أَنْفُسِكُمْ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" tooltip="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:19px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Separated&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:4px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;All of these conditions apply, top box first:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Vowel Lengthening: A long vowel or a soft letter is held.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Secondary: The lengthening has a cause, one of two: a hamzah right before or right after the letter, or a sukūn on the next letter.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Caused by hamzah: The cause is a hamzah right before or right after the letter, and the letter is a long vowel.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Hamzah after: The hamzah comes right after the long vowel.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Separated:&lt;/b&gt; The hamzah begins the next word: the long vowel ends one word, and you do not stop between them.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Length:&lt;/b&gt; 4 or 5 counts, set by the box “Hamzah after”.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:4px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Examples:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:30px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:19px;&quot;&gt;بِمَآ أُنْزِلَ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;alif · al-Baqarah 2:4&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:30px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:19px;&quot;&gt;قُوٓا أَنْفُسَكُمْ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;wāw · at-Taḥrīm 66:6&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:30px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:19px;&quot;&gt;وَفِيٓ أَنْفُسِكُمْ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;yāʾ · adh-Dhāriyāt 51:21&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:2px;&quot;&gt;If you stop on the first word, its long vowel is Natural, 2 counts. The muṣḥaf writes &lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:17px;&quot;&gt;يَآ أَيُّهَا&lt;/span&gt; joined, but it is two words, and you cannot stop on &lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:17px;&quot;&gt;يَا&lt;/span&gt;. The long vowel heard after the pronoun &lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:17px;&quot;&gt;هُ&lt;/span&gt; or &lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:17px;&quot;&gt;هِ&lt;/span&gt; also counts when a hamzah follows, as in &lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:17px;&quot;&gt;مَالَهُۥٓ أَخْلَدَهُ&lt;/span&gt; (al-Humazah 104:3); if you stop on that word, this vowel is not read at all.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" id="munfasil">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=28;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F6B93B;strokeColor=#FAD893;strokeWidth=2;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#0B1324;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=10;shadow=0;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="230" width="360" x="440" y="1400" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="&lt;div style=&quot;width:336px;height:210px;color:#0B1324;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:36px;line-height:36px;font-size:30px;font-weight:bold;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;Hamzah before&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:18px;font-weight:normal;&quot;&gt; (Substituted)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;height:44px;line-height:44px;font-size:32px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;الهمز قبل حرف المدّ (البدل)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:24px;margin:6px 0px 8px 0px;display:flex;align-items:center;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;flex:1;height:1px;background-color:#826730;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;flex:none;box-sizing:border-box;width:132px;height:24px;line-height:24px;border-radius:12px;background-color:#0B1324;color:#F6B93B;font-size:14px;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;2 counts&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;flex:1;height:1px;background-color:#826730;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:92px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;justify-content:center;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:14px;line-height:20px;text-align:center;text-wrap:balance;&quot;&gt;The hamzah comes right before the long vowel, in the same word, and no hamzah or sukūn comes right after the long vowel.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:30px;line-height:30px;margin-top:2px;text-align:center;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:13px;font-style:italic;margin-right:10px;&quot;&gt;like&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;unicode-bidi:isolate;font-size:20px;&quot;&gt;ءَادَمَ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:20px;margin:0px 10px;&quot;&gt;·&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;unicode-bidi:isolate;font-size:20px;&quot;&gt;أُوتِيَ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:20px;margin:0px 10px;&quot;&gt;·&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;unicode-bidi:isolate;font-size:20px;&quot;&gt;إِيمَانًا&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" tooltip="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:19px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Hamzah before (Substituted)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:4px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;All of these conditions apply, top box first:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Vowel Lengthening: A long vowel or a soft letter is held.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Secondary: The lengthening has a cause, one of two: a hamzah right before or right after the letter, or a sukūn on the next letter.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Caused by hamzah: The cause is a hamzah right before or right after the letter, and the letter is a long vowel.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Hamzah before (Substituted):&lt;/b&gt; The hamzah comes right before the long vowel, in the same word, and no hamzah or sukūn comes right after the long vowel.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Length:&lt;/b&gt; 2 counts.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:4px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Examples:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:30px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:19px;&quot;&gt;ءَادَمَ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;alif · al-Baqarah 2:31&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:30px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:19px;&quot;&gt;أُوتِيَ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;wāw · al-Baqarah 2:136&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:30px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:19px;&quot;&gt;إِيمَانًا&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;yāʾ · Āl ʿImrān 3:173&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:2px;&quot;&gt;In &lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:17px;&quot;&gt;إِيمَانًا&lt;/span&gt; only the yāʾ is Substituted. The alif after the mīm is Natural. The name Substituted (&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:17px;&quot;&gt;البدل&lt;/span&gt;): in most words of this kind the long vowel stands in place of a second hamzah, as &lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:17px;&quot;&gt;ءَادَمَ&lt;/span&gt; was &lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:17px;&quot;&gt;أَأْدَمَ&lt;/span&gt;. In a few, such as &lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:17px;&quot;&gt;قُرْءَان&lt;/span&gt;, the long vowel is original; they are read the same.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" id="badal">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=28;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F6B93B;strokeColor=#FAD893;strokeWidth=2;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#0B1324;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=10;shadow=0;gradientColor=#F4846B;gradientDirection=south;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="230" width="360" x="640" y="1110" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="&lt;div style=&quot;width:336px;height:210px;color:#0B1324;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:36px;line-height:36px;font-size:30px;font-weight:bold;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;Required&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;height:44px;line-height:44px;font-size:32px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;اللازم&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:24px;margin:6px 0px 8px 0px;display:flex;align-items:center;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;flex:1;height:1px;background-color:#3A5F85;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;flex:none;box-sizing:border-box;width:132px;height:24px;line-height:24px;border-radius:12px;background-color:#0B1324;color:#6FB5F3;font-size:14px;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;6 counts&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;flex:1;height:1px;background-color:#3A5F85;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:92px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;justify-content:center;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:14px;line-height:20px;text-align:center;text-wrap:balance;&quot;&gt;The sukūn is permanent. It is there whether you stop on the word or do not stop.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:30px;line-height:30px;margin-top:2px;text-align:center;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:13px;font-style:italic;margin-right:10px;&quot;&gt;like&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;unicode-bidi:isolate;font-size:20px;&quot;&gt;الْحَآقَّةُ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:20px;margin:0px 10px;&quot;&gt;·&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;unicode-bidi:isolate;font-size:20px;&quot;&gt;ءَآلْءَانَ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:20px;margin:0px 10px;&quot;&gt;·&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;unicode-bidi:isolate;font-size:20px;&quot;&gt;قٓ = قَافْ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" tooltip="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:19px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Required&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:4px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;All of these conditions apply, top box first:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Vowel Lengthening: A long vowel or a soft letter is held.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Secondary: The lengthening has a cause, one of two: a hamzah right before or right after the letter, or a sukūn on the next letter.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Caused by sukūn: The cause is a sukūn on the next letter.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Required:&lt;/b&gt; The sukūn is permanent. It is there whether you stop on the word or do not stop.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Length:&lt;/b&gt; 6 counts.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:4px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Examples:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:30px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:19px;&quot;&gt;الضَّآلِّينَ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;In a word (the alif) · al-Fātiḥah 1:7&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:30px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:19px;&quot;&gt;قٓ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;In a letter name · Qāf 50:1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:2px;&quot;&gt;The 6 counts have exceptions. They are given under Heavy (in a word), Light (in a word) and Light (in a letter name).&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" id="lazim">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=28;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#6FB5F3;strokeColor=#B0D6F8;strokeWidth=2;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#0B1324;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=10;shadow=0;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="230" width="360" x="1240" y="1110" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="&lt;div style=&quot;width:336px;height:210px;color:#0B1324;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:36px;line-height:36px;font-size:30px;font-weight:bold;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;Optional&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:18px;font-weight:normal;&quot;&gt; (At a stop)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;height:44px;line-height:44px;font-size:32px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;العارض للسكون&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:24px;margin:6px 0px 8px 0px;display:flex;align-items:center;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;flex:1;height:1px;background-color:#3A5F85;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;flex:none;box-sizing:border-box;width:132px;height:24px;line-height:24px;border-radius:12px;background-color:#0B1324;color:#6FB5F3;font-size:14px;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;2, 4 or 6 counts&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;flex:1;height:1px;background-color:#3A5F85;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:92px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;justify-content:center;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:14px;line-height:20px;text-align:center;text-wrap:balance;&quot;&gt;The sukūn is not permanent. It is there only when you stop on the word.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:30px;line-height:30px;margin-top:2px;text-align:center;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:13px;font-style:italic;margin-right:10px;&quot;&gt;like&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;unicode-bidi:isolate;font-size:20px;&quot;&gt;نَسْتَعِينُ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:20px;margin:0px 10px;&quot;&gt;·&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;unicode-bidi:isolate;font-size:20px;&quot;&gt;الْمُفْلِحُونَ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:20px;margin:0px 10px;&quot;&gt;·&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;unicode-bidi:isolate;font-size:20px;&quot;&gt;خَوْفٍ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" tooltip="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:19px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Optional (At a stop)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:4px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;All of these conditions apply, top box first:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Vowel Lengthening: A long vowel or a soft letter is held.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Secondary: The lengthening has a cause, one of two: a hamzah right before or right after the letter, or a sukūn on the next letter.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Caused by sukūn: The cause is a sukūn on the next letter.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Optional (At a stop):&lt;/b&gt; The sukūn is not permanent. It is there only when you stop on the word.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Length:&lt;/b&gt; 2, 4 or 6 counts.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:4px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Examples:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:30px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:19px;&quot;&gt;الْمُفْلِحُونَ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Long vowel: wāw · al-Baqarah 2:5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:30px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:19px;&quot;&gt;خَوْفٍ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Soft letter: wāw after a fatḥah · Quraysh 106:4&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:2px;&quot;&gt;If the letter you stop on is a hamzah right after a long vowel, as in &lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:17px;&quot;&gt;السَّمَآءِ&lt;/span&gt;, the kind is Connected and 2 counts is not allowed. Keep one length for every long vowel you stop on in a recitation, and one for every soft letter. The soft letter may be as long as the long vowel or shorter, never longer.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" id="arid">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=28;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#6FB5F3;strokeColor=#B0D6F8;strokeWidth=2;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#0B1324;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=10;shadow=0;gradientColor=#7FE3CF;gradientDirection=south;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="230" width="360" x="2240" y="1110" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="&lt;div style=&quot;width:336px;height:210px;color:#0B1324;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:36px;line-height:36px;font-size:30px;font-weight:bold;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;Long vowel&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;height:44px;line-height:44px;font-size:32px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;حرف المدّ&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:24px;margin:6px 0px 8px 0px;display:flex;align-items:center;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;flex:1;height:1px;background-color:#3A5F85;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;flex:none;box-sizing:border-box;width:132px;height:24px;line-height:20px;border-radius:12px;border:2px solid #0B1324;color:#0B1324;font-size:14px;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;2, 4 or 6 counts&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;flex:1;height:1px;background-color:#3A5F85;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:92px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;justify-content:center;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:14px;line-height:20px;text-align:center;text-wrap:balance;&quot;&gt;The letter is a long vowel.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:30px;line-height:30px;margin-top:2px;text-align:center;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:13px;font-style:italic;margin-right:10px;&quot;&gt;like&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;unicode-bidi:isolate;font-size:20px;&quot;&gt;الْبَيَانَ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:20px;margin:0px 10px;&quot;&gt;·&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;unicode-bidi:isolate;font-size:20px;&quot;&gt;الْمُفْلِحُونَ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:20px;margin:0px 10px;&quot;&gt;·&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;unicode-bidi:isolate;font-size:20px;&quot;&gt;نَسْتَعِينُ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" tooltip="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:19px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Long vowel&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:4px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;All of these conditions apply, top box first:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Vowel Lengthening: A long vowel or a soft letter is held.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Secondary: The lengthening has a cause, one of two: a hamzah right before or right after the letter, or a sukūn on the next letter.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Caused by sukūn: The cause is a sukūn on the next letter.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Optional (At a stop): The sukūn is not permanent. It is there only when you stop on the word.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Long vowel:&lt;/b&gt; The letter is a long vowel.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Length:&lt;/b&gt; 2, 4 or 6 counts, set by the box “Optional (At a stop)”.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:4px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Examples:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:30px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:19px;&quot;&gt;الْبَيَانَ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;alif · ar-Raḥmān 55:4&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:30px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:19px;&quot;&gt;الْمُفْلِحُونَ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;wāw · al-Baqarah 2:5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:30px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:19px;&quot;&gt;نَسْتَعِينُ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;yāʾ · al-Fātiḥah 1:5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:2px;&quot;&gt;If you do not stop on the word, the long vowel is Natural, 2 counts.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" id="arid_madd">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=28;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#6FB5F3;strokeColor=#B0D6F8;strokeWidth=2;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#0B1324;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=10;shadow=0;gradientColor=#7FE3CF;gradientDirection=south;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="230" width="360" x="2040" y="1400" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="&lt;div style=&quot;width:336px;height:210px;color:#0B1324;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:36px;line-height:36px;font-size:30px;font-weight:bold;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;Soft letter&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;height:44px;line-height:44px;font-size:32px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;حرف اللين&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:24px;margin:6px 0px 8px 0px;display:flex;align-items:center;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;flex:1;height:1px;background-color:#3A5F85;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;flex:none;box-sizing:border-box;width:132px;height:24px;line-height:20px;border-radius:12px;border:2px solid #0B1324;color:#0B1324;font-size:14px;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;2, 4 or 6 counts&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;flex:1;height:1px;background-color:#3A5F85;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:92px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;justify-content:center;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:14px;line-height:20px;text-align:center;text-wrap:balance;&quot;&gt;The letter is a soft letter: wāw or yā&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&#39;Lucida Sans Unicode&#39;,&#39;Lucida Grande&#39;,Tahoma,sans-serif;&quot;&gt;ʾ&lt;/span&gt; with sukūn after a fatḥah.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:30px;line-height:30px;margin-top:2px;text-align:center;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:13px;font-style:italic;margin-right:10px;&quot;&gt;like&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;unicode-bidi:isolate;font-size:20px;&quot;&gt;خَوْفٍ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:20px;margin:0px 10px;&quot;&gt;·&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;unicode-bidi:isolate;font-size:20px;&quot;&gt;الْبَيْتِ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:20px;margin:0px 10px;&quot;&gt;·&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;unicode-bidi:isolate;font-size:20px;&quot;&gt;قُرَيْشٍ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" tooltip="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:19px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Soft letter&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:4px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;All of these conditions apply, top box first:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Vowel Lengthening: A long vowel or a soft letter is held.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Secondary: The lengthening has a cause, one of two: a hamzah right before or right after the letter, or a sukūn on the next letter.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Caused by sukūn: The cause is a sukūn on the next letter.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Optional (At a stop): The sukūn is not permanent. It is there only when you stop on the word.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Soft letter:&lt;/b&gt; The letter is a soft letter: wāw or yāʾ with sukūn after a fatḥah.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Length:&lt;/b&gt; 2, 4 or 6 counts, set by the box “Optional (At a stop)”.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:4px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Examples:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:30px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:19px;&quot;&gt;خَوْفٍ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;wāw · Quraysh 106:4&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:30px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:19px;&quot;&gt;الْبَيْتِ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;yāʾ · Quraysh 106:3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:30px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:19px;&quot;&gt;قُرَيْشٍ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;yāʾ · Quraysh 106:1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:2px;&quot;&gt;If you do not stop on the word, nothing is lengthened.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" id="lin">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=28;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#6FB5F3;strokeColor=#B0D6F8;strokeWidth=2;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#0B1324;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=10;shadow=0;gradientColor=#7FE3CF;gradientDirection=south;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="230" width="360" x="2440" y="1400" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="&lt;div style=&quot;width:336px;height:210px;color:#0B1324;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:36px;line-height:36px;font-size:30px;font-weight:bold;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;In a word&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;height:44px;line-height:44px;font-size:32px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;الكلمي&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:24px;margin:6px 0px 8px 0px;display:flex;align-items:center;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;flex:1;height:1px;background-color:#3A5F85;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;flex:none;box-sizing:border-box;width:132px;height:24px;line-height:20px;border-radius:12px;border:2px solid #0B1324;color:#0B1324;font-size:14px;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;6 counts&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;flex:1;height:1px;background-color:#3A5F85;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:92px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;justify-content:center;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:14px;line-height:20px;text-align:center;text-wrap:balance;&quot;&gt;The letter is a long vowel. It and the permanent sukūn are in the same word, and the word is not the name of a letter.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:30px;line-height:30px;margin-top:2px;text-align:center;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:13px;font-style:italic;margin-right:10px;&quot;&gt;like&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;unicode-bidi:isolate;font-size:20px;&quot;&gt;الْحَآقَّةُ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:20px;margin:0px 10px;&quot;&gt;·&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;unicode-bidi:isolate;font-size:20px;&quot;&gt;الضَّآلِّينَ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:20px;margin:0px 10px;&quot;&gt;·&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;unicode-bidi:isolate;font-size:20px;&quot;&gt;ءَآلْءَانَ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" tooltip="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:19px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;In a word&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:4px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;All of these conditions apply, top box first:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Vowel Lengthening: A long vowel or a soft letter is held.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Secondary: The lengthening has a cause, one of two: a hamzah right before or right after the letter, or a sukūn on the next letter.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Caused by sukūn: The cause is a sukūn on the next letter.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Required: The sukūn is permanent. It is there whether you stop on the word or do not stop.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;In a word:&lt;/b&gt; The letter is a long vowel. It and the permanent sukūn are in the same word, and the word is not the name of a letter.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Length:&lt;/b&gt; 6 counts, set by the box “Required”.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:4px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Examples:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:30px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:19px;&quot;&gt;الْحَآقَّةُ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Heavy: the qāf is doubled · al-Ḥāqqah 69:1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:30px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:19px;&quot;&gt;ءَآلْءَانَ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Light: the lām is not doubled · Yūnus 10:51&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:2px;&quot;&gt;When a long vowel ends one word and the next word begins with a sukūn, as in &lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:17px;&quot;&gt;فِي الْأَرْضِ&lt;/span&gt;, the long vowel is dropped and nothing is lengthened.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" id="kalimi">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=28;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#6FB5F3;strokeColor=#B0D6F8;strokeWidth=2;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#0B1324;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=10;shadow=0;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="230" width="360" x="1040" y="1400" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="&lt;div style=&quot;width:336px;height:210px;color:#0B1324;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:36px;line-height:36px;font-size:30px;font-weight:bold;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;In a letter name&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;height:44px;line-height:44px;font-size:32px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;الحرفي&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:24px;margin:6px 0px 8px 0px;display:flex;align-items:center;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;flex:1;height:1px;background-color:#3A5F85;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;flex:none;box-sizing:border-box;width:132px;height:24px;line-height:20px;border-radius:12px;border:2px solid #0B1324;color:#0B1324;font-size:14px;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;6 counts&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;flex:1;height:1px;background-color:#3A5F85;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:92px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;justify-content:center;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:14px;line-height:20px;text-align:center;text-wrap:balance;&quot;&gt;The held letter and the permanent sukūn are inside the three-letter name of one of the letters at the opening of a sūrah.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:30px;line-height:30px;margin-top:2px;text-align:center;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:13px;font-style:italic;margin-right:10px;&quot;&gt;like&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;unicode-bidi:isolate;font-size:20px;&quot;&gt;قٓ = قَافْ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:20px;margin:0px 10px;&quot;&gt;·&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;unicode-bidi:isolate;font-size:20px;&quot;&gt;مٓ = مِيمْ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" tooltip="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:19px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;In a letter name&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:4px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;All of these conditions apply, top box first:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Vowel Lengthening: A long vowel or a soft letter is held.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Secondary: The lengthening has a cause, one of two: a hamzah right before or right after the letter, or a sukūn on the next letter.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Caused by sukūn: The cause is a sukūn on the next letter.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Required: The sukūn is permanent. It is there whether you stop on the word or do not stop.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;In a letter name:&lt;/b&gt; The held letter and the permanent sukūn are inside the name of one of the letters at the opening of a sūrah (&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:17px;&quot;&gt;قٓ&lt;/span&gt; is read &lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:17px;&quot;&gt;قَافْ&lt;/span&gt;). The name has three letters: the middle one is the letter that is held, and the last one carries the sukūn. Only the eight letters of &lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:17px;&quot;&gt;كم عسل نقص&lt;/span&gt; have such a name.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Length:&lt;/b&gt; 6 counts, set by the box “Required”.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:4px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Examples:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:30px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:19px;&quot;&gt;لام «الٓمٓ»&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Heavy: lām into mīm · al-Baqarah 2:1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:30px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:19px;&quot;&gt;قٓ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Light: nothing to merge into · Qāf 50:1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:2px;&quot;&gt;Seven of the eight names have a long vowel in the middle; the name of &lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:17px;&quot;&gt;ع&lt;/span&gt; has a soft letter. Alif also opens sūrahs, but its name has no long vowel in the middle, so it is not lengthened. The five letters of &lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:17px;&quot;&gt;حي طهر&lt;/span&gt; have two-letter names with no sukūn at the end, so they are Natural, 2 counts.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" id="harfi">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=28;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#6FB5F3;strokeColor=#B0D6F8;strokeWidth=2;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#0B1324;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=10;shadow=0;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="230" width="360" x="1440" y="1400" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="&lt;div style=&quot;width:336px;height:210px;color:#0B1324;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:36px;line-height:36px;font-size:30px;font-weight:bold;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;Heavy&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;height:44px;line-height:44px;font-size:32px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;المثقّل&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:24px;margin:6px 0px 8px 0px;display:flex;align-items:center;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;flex:1;height:1px;background-color:#3A5F85;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;flex:none;box-sizing:border-box;width:132px;height:24px;line-height:20px;border-radius:12px;border:2px solid #0B1324;color:#0B1324;font-size:14px;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;6 counts&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;flex:1;height:1px;background-color:#3A5F85;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:92px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;justify-content:center;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:14px;line-height:20px;text-align:center;text-wrap:balance;&quot;&gt;The next letter is doubled, and the first of the two carries the sukūn.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:30px;line-height:30px;margin-top:2px;text-align:center;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:13px;font-style:italic;margin-right:10px;&quot;&gt;like&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;unicode-bidi:isolate;font-size:20px;&quot;&gt;الْحَآقَّةُ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:20px;margin:0px 10px;&quot;&gt;·&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;unicode-bidi:isolate;font-size:20px;&quot;&gt;الطَّآمَّةُ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:20px;margin:0px 10px;&quot;&gt;·&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;unicode-bidi:isolate;font-size:20px;&quot;&gt;الضَّآلِّينَ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" tooltip="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:19px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Heavy (in a word)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:4px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;All of these conditions apply, top box first:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Vowel Lengthening: A long vowel or a soft letter is held.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Secondary: The lengthening has a cause, one of two: a hamzah right before or right after the letter, or a sukūn on the next letter.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Caused by sukūn: The cause is a sukūn on the next letter.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Required: The sukūn is permanent. It is there whether you stop on the word or do not stop.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;In a word: The letter is a long vowel. It and the permanent sukūn are in the same word, and the word is not the name of a letter.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Heavy:&lt;/b&gt; The next letter is doubled, and the first of the two carries the sukūn.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Length:&lt;/b&gt; 6 counts, set by the box “Required”.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:4px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Examples:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:30px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:19px;&quot;&gt;الْحَآقَّةُ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;alif · al-Ḥāqqah 69:1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:30px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:19px;&quot;&gt;الطَّآمَّةُ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;alif · an-Nāziʿāt 79:34&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:30px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:19px;&quot;&gt;أَتُحَآجُّوٓنِّي&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;alif and wāw · al-Anʿām 6:80&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:2px;&quot;&gt;The Qurʾān has no example of this kind with yāʾ. One exception to the 6 counts: two words of this kind, &lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:17px;&quot;&gt;ءَآلذَّكَرَيْنِ&lt;/span&gt; (al-Anʿām 6:143, 144) and &lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:17px;&quot;&gt;ءَآللَّهُ&lt;/span&gt; (Yūnus 10:59, an-Naml 27:59), may also be read with an eased hamzah (&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:17px;&quot;&gt;تسهيل&lt;/span&gt;) and no lengthening; 6 counts is preferred.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" id="km">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=28;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#6FB5F3;strokeColor=#B0D6F8;strokeWidth=2;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#0B1324;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=10;shadow=0;gradientColor=#B49CF3;gradientDirection=south;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="230" width="360" x="640" y="1690" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="&lt;div style=&quot;width:336px;height:210px;color:#0B1324;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:36px;line-height:36px;font-size:30px;font-weight:bold;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;Light&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;height:44px;line-height:44px;font-size:32px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;المخفّف&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:24px;margin:6px 0px 8px 0px;display:flex;align-items:center;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;flex:1;height:1px;background-color:#3A5F85;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;flex:none;box-sizing:border-box;width:132px;height:24px;line-height:20px;border-radius:12px;border:2px solid #0B1324;color:#0B1324;font-size:14px;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;6 counts&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;flex:1;height:1px;background-color:#3A5F85;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:92px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;justify-content:center;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:14px;line-height:20px;text-align:center;text-wrap:balance;&quot;&gt;The next letter is not doubled, and it carries the sukūn itself.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:30px;line-height:30px;margin-top:2px;text-align:center;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:13px;font-style:italic;margin-right:10px;&quot;&gt;only in&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;unicode-bidi:isolate;font-size:20px;&quot;&gt;ءَآلْءَانَ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:13px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;(the first alif · Yūnus 10:51 and 10:91)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" tooltip="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:19px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Light (in a word)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:4px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;All of these conditions apply, top box first:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Vowel Lengthening: A long vowel or a soft letter is held.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Secondary: The lengthening has a cause, one of two: a hamzah right before or right after the letter, or a sukūn on the next letter.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Caused by sukūn: The cause is a sukūn on the next letter.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Required: The sukūn is permanent. It is there whether you stop on the word or do not stop.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;In a word: The letter is a long vowel. It and the permanent sukūn are in the same word, and the word is not the name of a letter.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Light:&lt;/b&gt; The next letter is not doubled, and it carries the sukūn itself.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Length:&lt;/b&gt; 6 counts, set by the box “Required”.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:4px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Examples:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:30px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:19px;&quot;&gt;ءَآلْءَانَ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;the first alif · Yūnus 10:51 and 10:91&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:2px;&quot;&gt;This is the only word of this kind in the reading of Ḥafṣ. One exception to the 6 counts: it may also be read with an eased hamzah (&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:17px;&quot;&gt;تسهيل&lt;/span&gt;) and no lengthening; 6 counts is preferred.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" id="kk">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=28;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#6FB5F3;strokeColor=#B0D6F8;strokeWidth=2;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#0B1324;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=10;shadow=0;gradientColor=#F2F7FF;gradientDirection=south;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="230" width="360" x="1040" y="1690" as="geometry" />
