        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="&lt;div style=&quot;width:336px;height:210px;color:#0B1324;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:36px;line-height:36px;font-size:30px;font-weight:bold;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;Heavy&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;height:44px;line-height:44px;font-size:32px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;المثقّل&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:24px;margin:6px 0px 8px 0px;display:flex;align-items:center;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;flex:1;height:1px;background-color:#3A5F85;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;flex:none;box-sizing:border-box;width:132px;height:24px;line-height:20px;border-radius:12px;border:2px solid #0B1324;color:#0B1324;font-size:14px;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;6 counts&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;flex:1;height:1px;background-color:#3A5F85;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:92px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;justify-content:center;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:14px;line-height:20px;text-align:center;text-wrap:balance;&quot;&gt;The last letter of the name, which has the sukūn, merges into the first letter of the next name.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:30px;line-height:30px;margin-top:2px;text-align:center;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:13px;font-style:italic;margin-right:10px;&quot;&gt;like&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;unicode-bidi:isolate;font-size:20px;&quot;&gt;لام «الٓمٓ»&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:20px;margin:0px 10px;&quot;&gt;·&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;unicode-bidi:isolate;font-size:20px;&quot;&gt;لام «الٓمٓصٓ»&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:20px;margin:0px 10px;&quot;&gt;·&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;unicode-bidi:isolate;font-size:20px;&quot;&gt;سين «طسٓمٓ»&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" tooltip="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:19px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Heavy (in a letter name)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:4px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;All of these conditions apply, top box first:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Vowel Lengthening: A long vowel or a soft letter is held.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Secondary: The lengthening has a cause, one of two: a hamzah right before or right after the letter, or a sukūn on the next letter.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Caused by sukūn: The cause is a sukūn on the next letter.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Required: The sukūn is permanent. It is there whether you stop on the word or do not stop.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;In a letter name: The held letter and the permanent sukūn are inside the three-letter name of one of the letters at the opening of a sūrah.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Heavy:&lt;/b&gt; The last letter of the name, which has the sukūn, merges into the first letter of the next name.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Length:&lt;/b&gt; 6 counts, set by the box “Required”.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:4px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Examples:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:30px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:19px;&quot;&gt;لام «الٓمٓ»&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;lām into mīm · al-Baqarah 2:1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:30px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:19px;&quot;&gt;لام «الٓمٓصٓ»&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;lām into mīm · al-Aʿrāf 7:1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:30px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:19px;&quot;&gt;سين «طسٓمٓ»&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;sīn into mīm · ash-Shuʿarāʾ 26:1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:2px;&quot;&gt;In &lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:17px;&quot;&gt;الٓمٓ&lt;/span&gt; the m that ends lām merges into the m that begins mīm, so the lām is Heavy. The mīm of &lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:17px;&quot;&gt;الٓمٓ&lt;/span&gt; is Light.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" id="hm">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=28;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#6FB5F3;strokeColor=#B0D6F8;strokeWidth=2;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#0B1324;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=10;shadow=0;gradientColor=#B49CF3;gradientDirection=south;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="230" width="360" x="1440" y="1690" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="&lt;div style=&quot;width:336px;height:210px;color:#0B1324;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:36px;line-height:36px;font-size:30px;font-weight:bold;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;Light&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;height:44px;line-height:44px;font-size:32px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;المخفّف&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:24px;margin:6px 0px 8px 0px;display:flex;align-items:center;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;flex:1;height:1px;background-color:#3A5F85;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;flex:none;box-sizing:border-box;width:132px;height:24px;line-height:20px;border-radius:12px;border:2px solid #0B1324;color:#0B1324;font-size:14px;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;6 counts&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;flex:1;height:1px;background-color:#3A5F85;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:92px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;justify-content:center;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:14px;line-height:20px;text-align:center;text-wrap:balance;&quot;&gt;The last letter of the name, which has the sukūn, does not merge into the letter after it.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;height:30px;line-height:30px;margin-top:2px;text-align:center;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:13px;font-style:italic;margin-right:10px;&quot;&gt;like&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;unicode-bidi:isolate;font-size:20px;&quot;&gt;قٓ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:20px;margin:0px 10px;&quot;&gt;·&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;unicode-bidi:isolate;font-size:20px;&quot;&gt;صٓ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:20px;margin:0px 10px;&quot;&gt;·&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;direction:rtl;unicode-bidi:isolate;font-size:20px;&quot;&gt;نٓ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" tooltip="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:19px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Light (in a letter name)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:4px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;All of these conditions apply, top box first:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Vowel Lengthening: A long vowel or a soft letter is held.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Secondary: The lengthening has a cause, one of two: a hamzah right before or right after the letter, or a sukūn on the next letter.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Caused by sukūn: The cause is a sukūn on the next letter.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Required: The sukūn is permanent. It is there whether you stop on the word or do not stop.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;In a letter name: The held letter and the permanent sukūn are inside the three-letter name of one of the letters at the opening of a sūrah.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Light:&lt;/b&gt; The last letter of the name, which has the sukūn, does not merge into the letter after it.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Length:&lt;/b&gt; 6 counts, set by the box “Required”.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:4px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Examples:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:30px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:19px;&quot;&gt;قٓ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Qāf 50:1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:30px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:19px;&quot;&gt;صٓ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;Ṣād 38:1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:30px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:19px;&quot;&gt;نٓ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;al-Qalam 68:1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:30px;white-space:nowrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:19px;&quot;&gt;ميم «الٓمٓ»&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;al-Baqarah 2:1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:2px;&quot;&gt;Two exceptions to the 6 counts. The name of &lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:17px;&quot;&gt;ع&lt;/span&gt;, in &lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:17px;&quot;&gt;كٓهيعٓصٓ&lt;/span&gt; and &lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:17px;&quot;&gt;عٓسٓقٓ&lt;/span&gt;, has a soft letter, not a long vowel, and may be read with 4 or 6 counts; 6 is preferred. The mīm of &lt;span dir=&quot;rtl&quot; style=&quot;font-size:17px;&quot;&gt;الٓمٓ&lt;/span&gt; at Āl ʿImrān 3:1 may be read with 6 or 2 counts if you do not stop on it, because a fatḥah then replaces its sukūn.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" id="hk">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=28;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#6FB5F3;strokeColor=#B0D6F8;strokeWidth=2;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontColor=#0B1324;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=10;shadow=0;gradientColor=#F2F7FF;gradientDirection=south;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="230" width="360" x="1840" y="1690" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="legend-natural" connectable="0" parent="1" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=28;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#B2E7B6;strokeColor=#D5F2D7;strokeWidth=2;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=20;fontColor=#0B1324;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=4;shadow=0;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;height: 20px; line-height: 20px; font-size: 20px; font-weight: bold; color: rgb(11, 19, 36); white-space: nowrap;&quot;&gt;no cause&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
